message: "If you cite this computational research thesis, please use the metadata below. No DOI is minted here; do not invent one."
type: thesis
title: "Complexity Science and NSTG-Guided In-Silico Pathology Dynamics for Biologics Pathway Exploration"
authors:
  - family-names: Ogbonna
    given-names: Kelechi Emeka
abstract: >-
  Complex pathological systems sit in Weaver's class of organised complexity.
  This computational research thesis — not a clinical study, not a medical
  device — specifies a data-only in-silico pipeline in which a YAML CaseCard
  holds knowledge, evidence pointers, candidate mechanisms, falsifiers, and
  qualitative Nigeria Standard Treatment Guidelines (NSTG) constraints.
  NSTG is a knowledge constraint, not a source of ODE coefficients, doses, or
  predictions. Headed sections state the Problem Statement, Justification of
  the Study, and Significance of the Study. The evidence gate never opens.
keywords:
  - complexity science
  - in-silico pathology
  - NSTG
  - CaseCard
  - PathwaySketch
  - knowledge constraint
  - parameter smuggling
  - biologics pathway exploration
